<title>USA: U.S. Energy Systems Q1 shr loss decreases.</title>
<headline>U.S. Energy Systems Q1 shr loss decreases.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PALM BEACH, Fla. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended April 30</p>
<p>						 1997	   1996</p>
<p> Revenues				 $375,000	$    --</p>
<p> Operating (loss)		    (154,000)    (221,000)</p>
<p> Loss from Joint Ventures	   (26,000)     (39,000)</p>
<p> Net (loss)			    (171,000)    (430,000)</p>
<p>Net (loss) applicable</p>
<p>  to common stock		    (171,000)    (444,000)</p>
<p> Net (loss) per common share	  (0.04)	 (1.01)</p>
<p> Weighted avg shrs outstanding   4,334,193	439,622</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
<p>NOTES: The full company name is U.S. Energy Systems Inc.</p>
<p>The company said Q1 loss was less than anticipated.</p>
<p>The company conducted an initial public offering in December 1996 that increased the company's number of shares outstanding by nearly ten-fold.</p>
